{title:Description}

{pstd}{cmd:pctrange} computes four percentile ranges of the s
variable(s): the 75-25 (interquartile) range, the 90-10, 95-0
ranges as well as the conventional range. These ranges are re
scalars.  If multiple variables are included in the {it:varli
are returned as a matrix.


{title:Options}

{phang}{opt noprint} specifies that the results are to be ret
but not printed.

{phang}{opt format(string)} specifies the format to be used
in displaying the matrix of percentile ranges for multiple va

{phang}{opt matrix(string)} specifies the name of the Stata m
to be created for multiple variables.


{title:Examples}

{phang}{stata "sysuse auto" : . sysuse auto}{p_end}
